# State of charge of a 12 V lead-acid battery, read from its resting voltage.
#
# Applied as a transform profile on the channel link, so fence_battery_soc
# actually holds the percentage rather than displaying one. That is what makes
# the battery icon right: Basic UI asks for the icon with the item's state, and
# a raw 13.1 V was read as 13 % and drew an almost flat battery on a full one.
#
# This is the standard open-circuit table for a 12 V lead-acid battery. It
# assumes the battery is at rest, and the fence battery is not: a solar panel
# feeds it, and any charge current lifts the terminal voltage above what the
# cells actually hold. So a reading over 12.62 V reports 100 % whether the
# battery is genuinely full or merely being charged -- which is why the volts
# stay one click away rather than being replaced by this.
#
# A battery under load reads the other way, lower than its true charge, so
# treat a dip during a cold night as a reading rather than as capacity lost.
[..11.40]=0
]11.40..11.58]=10
]11.58..11.75]=20
]11.75..11.90]=30
]11.90..12.06]=40
]12.06..12.20]=50
]12.20..12.32]=60
]12.32..12.42]=70
]12.42..12.50]=80
]12.50..12.62]=90
]12.62..]=100
